.SS "int32_t schultz_selection_area_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Makes a selection area\&. The node itself draws nothing and takes no room of its own\&. Give it a pane and children like any other container\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to build in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The node to hang it from\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_selection_area_set_range (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP area, \fBschultz_handle\fP from, uint32_t from_at, \fBschultz_handle\fP to, uint32_t to_at)"

.PP
Sets where the selection starts and where it now ends\&. The two ends each name a node and a byte offset inside it\&. They may be the same node, and they may be given in either order: dragging backwards is an ordinary thing to do, so the area works out which comes first in reading order rather than asking the caller to\&.
.PP
Every selectable node in the area is then told its share, which is all of its text, part of it, or none\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the area\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarea\fP A node from schultz_selection_area_create\&. 
.br
\fIfrom\fP The node the selection started in\&. 
.br
\fIfrom_at\fP The byte offset it started at\&. 
.br
\fIto\fP The node it now ends in\&. 
.br
\fIto_at\fP The byte offset it now ends at\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the area is not one or when either end is not inside it\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_selection_area_ends (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP area, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_from, uint32_t * out_from_at, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_to, uint32_t * out_to_at)"

.PP
Where the selection starts and ends, in reading order\&. Named for the question rather than as the mirror of the setter, because what comes back is sorted and what went in need not have been\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the area\&. NULL yields an error\&. 
.br
\fIarea\fP A node from schultz_selection_area_create\&. 
.br
\fIout_from\fP Receives the earlier node\&. May be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIout_from_at\fP Receives its byte offset\&. May be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIout_to\fP Receives the later node\&. May be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIout_to_at\fP Receives its byte offset\&. May be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK when there is a selection, SCHULTZ_ERR_UNAVAILABLE when there is none, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBschultz_handle\fP schultz_selection_area_of (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

.PP
The nearest selection area above a node, or none\&. A widget asks this to find out whether it owns its own selection or takes part in somebody else's\&. A label inside an area lets a press go past it so that the area can run the drag; the same label on its own handles the press itself, as it always did\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. NULL yields SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP The node to look above\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The nearest ancestor area, or SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE when there is none\&. A node that is itself an area is not its own area\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_selection_area_copy (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP area, const \fBschultz_render_options\fP * options)"

.PP
Puts the selected text on the clipboard\&. The pieces in reading order, with a line break between the text of one widget and the next, because two paragraphs pasted together with nothing between them read as one\&.
.PP
When the selection holds a picture and render options are given, the picture is offered beside the text as image/png and image/bmp, built only if something asks\&. Pass NULL for the options to offer text alone\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the area\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarea\fP A node from schultz_selection_area_create\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP How to render a selected picture, or NULL for text alone\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE, SCHULTZ_ERR_UNAVAILABLE when nothing is selected, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const char * schultz_selection_area_text (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP area)"

.PP
The selected text, as one string\&. What a copy would put on the clipboard, for a host that wants it without involving the clipboard at all\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the area\&. NULL yields NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarea\fP A node from schultz_selection_area_create\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The text, NUL terminated, or NULL when nothing is selected\&. Owned by the area and valid until the selection changes\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_selection_area_set_limit (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP area, uint64_t bytes)"

.PP
The most bytes a copy out of this area may produce\&. Bytes rather than characters, because once a picture can be in a selection a character count stops describing what producing it costs\&. A page of text is kilobytes; one screenshot is megabytes\&.
.PP
The limit is on producing a result, not on what may be highlighted\&. Highlighting a long transcript is a walk; building the string, or the picture beside it, is the part that can hurt\&.
.PP
Twenty megabytes by default, which text never comes near: that is around twenty million characters, or a hundred thousand chat messages\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the area\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarea\fP A node from schultz_selection_area_create\&. 
.br
\fIbytes\fP The limit\&. Zero means no limit at all\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint64_t schultz_selection_area_limit (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP area)"

.PP
The limit a copy out of this area stops at\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the area\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.br
\fIarea\fP A node from schultz_selection_area_create\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The limit in bytes, or 0 when there is none\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_selection_area_was_cut (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP area)"

.PP
Whether the last copy stopped early because of the limit\&. Named for the question, because the answer is about what happened rather than about what was set\&. A host that gets a yes here has something to say to the person: what they copied is not all of what they selected\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the area\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.br
\fIarea\fP A node from schultz_selection_area_create\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Nonzero when the last text or copy was cut short\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_selection_area_picture (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP area, uint32_t format, const \fBschultz_render_options\fP * options, const void ** out_bytes, uint64_t * out_length)"

.PP
The selected picture, written out as a file, or nothing\&. A selection may cover a picture as well as text\&. Plain text has nowhere to put one, so it is offered separately and produced only when something asks for a format that can hold it\&.
.PP
The picture is rendered from the node rather than taken from anywhere, which is what lets a drawn canvas be copied as well as a loaded picture\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the area\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarea\fP A node from schultz_selection_area_create\&. 
.br
\fIformat\fP SCHULTZ_IMAGE_PNG or SCHULTZ_IMAGE_BMP\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP How to render it: the fonts, glyphs, images and resources a draw needs\&. Must not be NULL, because only the host has them\&. 
.br
\fIout_bytes\fP Receives the file's bytes\&. Must not be NULL\&. Owned by the toolkit and valid until the next picture is written\&. 
.br
\fIout_length\fP Receives how many bytes\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_UNAVAILABLE when no picture is selected or the result would pass the limit, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const char * schultz_selection_area_html (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP area)"

.PP
The selected content as HTML, keeping its formatting\&. What a copy offers beside the plain text, and what a word processor takes when it is given the choice\&. Each widget's share becomes a paragraph carrying its own size, colour and, when the face is a code face, a monospace family\&. A picture in the range is written into the document itself, so one format carries the whole selection rather than the text and one picture arriving separately\&.
.PP
The styles come from each widget's resolved style rather than from the theme, so a host that set a colour on one paragraph keeps it in the paste\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the area\&. NULL yields NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarea\fP A node from schultz_selection_area_create\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The markup, NUL terminated, or NULL when nothing is selected\&. Owned by the area and valid until the selection changes\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_selection_area_clear (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP area)"

.PP
Takes the selection away, leaving nothing selected anywhere in it\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the area\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarea\fP A node from schultz_selection_area_create\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

